    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-015",
      "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
      "finding": "Player BEST/AVOID tier tendency in H2 trigger games (55 series) was studied descriptively. Team AVOID% ranges 50.6% (ORL) to 6.8% (SAC); team BEST% 0.0%-15.8%."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-088",
      "status_as_recorded": "supported",
      "finding": "Connector absence displaces team offensive identity (D_A) more than usage-matched non-organizer absence. Unmatched conn vs role D_A 0.2020 vs 0.1021, t=5.97 p=2.87e-08. Usage-matched vs role: paired dD_A +0.1151, P(conn>ctrl)=81.2%, t=6.35 p=7.35e-09 n=96. Vs terminal: +0.0777 t=2.37 p=0.0261 n=25."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-036",
      "status_as_recorded": "supported",
      "finding": "The team-level BEST vs AVOID gap holds when H2 possessions are filtered to initiating player. Mean gap (n>=10 each tier) +0.427 PPP. Mean BEST 1.347 (38 players) vs AVOID 0.920 (94 players). Stars mean gap +0.542 (n=15) vs role +0.428 (n=16)."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-087",
      "status_as_recorded": "rejected",
      "finding": "Connector presence does not shield stars (dTS +0.05 pp p=0.937; dTO +0.74 pp p=0.00364, wrong sign for shielding). HasConn on-off PPP BOTH_NULL (mean -0.041 p=0.939, median +0.528 p=0.731, n=73). Lineup ORtg lift is a talent confound."
    }
  ],
  "failed_approaches": [
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-015",
      "what_failed": "Descriptive analysis of player BEST/AVOID tier tendency",
      "why": "No outcome test; player samples 10-178 possessions (E_unclear, sample size)."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-088",
      "what_failed": "Measuring offensive identity resilience for connectors",
      "why": "Limited by small sample (n=96 matched pairs vs role; n=25 vs terminal) and risk of mechanical floor."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-036",
      "what_failed": "Measuring player-level BEST vs AVOID PPP gap",
      "why": "Limited by small sample (only 3 players clear n>=30 both tiers; most star cells below n>=30 gate)."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-087",
      "what_failed": "Measuring connector tangible impact (star shielding, TO, lineup lift)",
      "why": "Failed to show hypothesized effects (powered null results for PPP/TS/eFG shielding, TO rate rises with connectors). Limited by confounding and small sample size."
    }
  ],
  "evidence_establishes": [
    "Player-specific analyses, especially those involving specific play types or context changes, frequently suffer from small sample sizes, making robust conclusions difficult (FAM:SF-APPS-015, FAM:SF-APPS-088, FAM:SF-APPS-036, FAM:SF-APPS-087).",
    "Confounding variables, particularly talent, pose a significant risk when attempting to isolate the impact of specific player roles on team outcomes (FAM:SF-APPS-087).",
    "The concept of 'offensive identity resilience' for certain player roles ('connectors') has been explored, suggesting that the absence of these players can displace team offensive identity (FAM:SF-APPS-088).",
    "Direct measures of 'tangible impact' for specific roles (e.g., star shielding, lineup lift) may not yield expected results or can be confounded (FAM:SF-APPS-087)."
  ],
  "evidence_does_not_establish": [
    "Validated definitions or methodologies for classifying 'cut-heavy' or 'drive-heavy' shapers.",
    "A direct comparison of the transferability of 'cut-heavy' versus 'drive-heavy' player roles.",
    "A robust and widely accepted methodology for quantifying 'role travel' or transferability.",
    "Whether specific offensive archetypes inherently 'travel better' than others."
