  },
  "prior_work": {
    "already_answered": "no",
    "cited": [
      "FAM:SF-APPS-088",
      "FAM:SF-APPS-087"
    ],
    "summary": "No prior work directly addresses the transferability of 'cut-heavy' vs 'drive-heavy' shapers' roles. However, related studies on player role impact and offensive identity for 'connectors' (FAM:SF-APPS-088, FAM:SF-APPS-087) highlight significant methodological challenges, including small sample sizes and confounding, which are highly relevant to this question. These studies indicate that robustly measuring player role impact and transferability is difficult."
  },
  "risks": [
    {
      "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
      "text": "The number of players identifiable as specific archetypes (cut-heavy, drive-heavy) who also have sufficient data points across different contexts (e.g., team changes, significant role shifts) will likely be very low, leading to underpowered tests."
