    "estimand": "The difference in the change in player offensive impact (e.g., adjusted PPP or team ORtg differential when on-court) for 'cut-heavy shapers' versus 'drive-heavy shapers' when moving to a new team or experiencing a significant role change, after controlling for talent and contextual factors.",
    "unit": "Player-season for archetype classification; player-transition (change of team/role) for outcome measurement.",
    "sample": "Identify all players who played at least 500 possessions in a season and changed teams between the 2022-23 and 2025-26 seasons, or had a significant change in offensive role (e.g., >20% change in usage rate or initiator rate) between consecutive seasons on the same team. Classify these players as 'cut-heavy shaper' or 'drive-heavy shaper' based on their play-type distribution (e.g., proportion of possessions ending in cuts vs. drives) in their initial context. Minimum of N=15 players per archetype group for a comparison, or N=50 for a single group analysis.",
    "power": "Target 80% power to detect a medium effect size (Cohen's d = 0.5) for the difference in role transferability. This implies a minimum sample size per group (cut-heavy vs drive-heavy) based on the chosen statistical test. A preliminary power analysis will be conducted once archetype and transition counts are known. Given historical data, achieving this power is a significant risk.",
    "controls": "Control for player talent (e.g., prior season's efficiency, All-Star selections), team quality (e.g., prior season's ORtg, net rating), teammate quality (e.g., average ORtg of other 4 players on court), and offensive system (e.g., team pace, play-type distribution, coach changes). Use a difference-in-differences approach or a fixed-effects model for players who transition.",
    "falsification": "A falsification test could involve examining whether the chosen impact metric for 'role travel' shows significant changes for players who did NOT change teams or roles, after controlling for year-over-year variation. A robust measure should show minimal 'travel' for stable roles/teams.",
    "multiplicity": "Given the likely small sample size, avoid multiple testing. Focus on a single primary outcome metric for 'role travel' (e.g., change in Net ORtg per 100 possessions when on-court, adjusted for teammates). If secondary metrics are explored, apply Bonferroni correction or report p-values with caution.",
    "decision_rule": "The hypothesis is supported if the mean change in offensive impact for 'cut-heavy shapers' is significantly greater than for 'drive-heavy shapers' (one-tailed t-test or regression coefficient, p < 0.05) after controlling for confounders, and the effect size is practically meaningful.",
    "data_version": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 regular seasons and playoffs; NBA 2025-26 regular season and playoffs (as available on 2026-08-08)."
  }
}

